eds receive appropriate nutritional support.", "RANSON:RANSON refers to a scoring system utilized to evaluate the severity of acute pancreatitis in patients. This system comprises a set of criteria that incorporates both clinical and laboratory findings, allowing healthcare professionals to assess the condition's seriousness effectively. The Ranson criteria are essential for guiding treatment decisions and predicting patient outcomes in cases of acute pancreatitis.", "APACHE II:APACHE II is a severity scoring system designed to evaluate the prognosis of critically ill patients, including those suffering from acute pancreatitis. This scoring system measures the severity of illness in patients, providing a quantitative assessment that helps in determining the risk of complications. Specifically, a score of 10 or higher on the APACHE II scale indicates an increased risk of adverse outcomes. The tool is widely utilized in clinical settings to guide treatment decisions and improve patient management for those in critical condition.", "SONDA DE ALIMENTACIÓN ENTERAL:La sonda de alimentación enteral es un dispositivo que se planea colocar para proporcionar nutrición al paciente de manera directa al yeyuno.", "OBESIDAD GRADO 1:", "NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL TOTAL (NPT):NPT es un tipo de nutrición administrada intravenosamente que el paciente ha estado recibiendo para mantener su estado nutricional.", "SONDA NASOENTERAL:The \"SONDA NASOENTERAL\" refers to a medical procedure involving the use of a nasoenteral tube, which is a type of feeding tube designed for providing enteral nutrition to patients who are unable to eat by mouth. This device is particularly indicated for short-term use and is beneficial for patients with issues such as delayed gastric emptying or a risk of aspiration. \n\nThe nasoenteral tube can be categorized into specific types, including the nasoduodenal (SND) and nasoyeyunal (SNY) tubes, which allow for the infusion of nutrition beyond the pylorus, directly into the stomach or intestines. While effective for delivering nutrition, the use of nasoenteral tubes can lead to complications and may cause agitation in patients with decreased consciousness. Overall, the SONDA NASOENTERAL serves as a critical tool in the management of patients requiring enteral feeding.", "TC (TOMOGRAFÍA COMPUTARIZADA):La TC es un procedimiento de imagen que se realizó para evaluar la evolución del paciente con pancreatitis aguda.", "VANCOMICINA:Vancomicina is a broad-spectrum antibiotic that has been administered empirically to patients during their treatment. It has been shown to increase the abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila in rodents, indicating its potential effects on gut microbiota.", "HEMOCULTIVO:El hemocultivo es una prueba que se realizó para detectar infecciones en el paciente, mostrando crecimiento de cocos gram positivos.", "GLUCEMIAS:GLUCEMIAS se refiere a las mediciones de los niveles de azúcar en la sangre. Estas mediciones son especialmente importantes en el contexto de pacientes con Alzheimer, ya que se utilizan para ajustar el tratamiento de la enfermedad.", "REPOSO PANCREÁTICO:El reposo pancreático es una estrategia terapéutica que se ha utilizado en el tratamiento de la pancreatitis, aunque su eficacia ha sido cuestionada.", "FALLO ORGÁNICO:FALLO ORGÁNICO refers to a serious condition characterized by the failure of one or more organs, which may require the use of specialized nutritional formulas to support the affected individual. This condition is particularly critical in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, where it can manifest as a severe complication. The presence of organ failure in these patients can extend beyond 48 hours and is associated with an increased mortality rate, especially in severe cases."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}